    {
      "id": "hft0a9k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Joint Sitting of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ekyfa8x",
      "content": "A joint sitting of both Houses may be called by the President when there is a deadlock between Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha over a bill. It is presided over by the Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "id": "g8ntaqg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Powers and Functions of Parliament"
    },
    {
      "id": "xkr72fh",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Legislative Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kf9ts1s",
      "content": "• Makes laws for the country"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "anxh1ia",
      "content": "• Amends the Constitution"
    },
    {
      "id": "8p8gufp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Financial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "j15w40u",
      "content": "• Approves the Union Budget"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "dkjxpbg",
      "content": "• Controls public expenditure"
    },
    {
      "id": "ei8gv7f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Executive Control"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yefz23g",
      "content": "• Council of Ministers responsible to Lok Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6wpsa6d",
      "content": "• Parliament can remove government through no-confidence motion"
    },
    {
      "id": "invocui",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Judicial Powers"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Money Bills (Article 110) can only be introduced in the Lok Sabha and require the prior recommendation of the President.",
        "The Speaker of the Lok Sabha presides over a Joint Sitting of Parliament, not the Vice President (Chairman of Rajya Sabha).",
        "Rajya Sabha enjoys exclusive powers under Article 249 to authorize Parliament to legislate on State List matters and Article 312 for All-India Services."
      ],
      "id": "b77m2mr"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8z83z4f",
      "content": "• Impeachment of President"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5k1dq2r",
      "content": "• Removal of judges of Supreme Court and High Courts"
    },
    {
      "id": "z0m4uoy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mgcqg04",
      "content": "• Parliament consists of President, Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "31sv6ur",
      "content": "• Lok Sabha maximum strength 552."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2zgdzt5",
      "content": "• Rajya Sabha maximum strength 250."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4lo8e6z",
      "content": "• Money Bill introduced only in Lok Sabha."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "17is2bo",
      "content": "• Joint sitting presided by Speaker of Lok Sabha."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
